course: dictionary
lesson: 3991
title: Gallon: a measure and a mighty exaggeration
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gallon is a unit for measuring liquids, like the amount of milk or petrol in a container. In the UK, one gallon holds 8 pints.
explain: The size of a gallon depends on where you are. A UK gallon is about 4.55 litres, but a US gallon is a little smaller, about 3.79 litres.
explain: People also use gallon in everyday talk to mean a huge amount. «She sheds gallons of tears, making a pool about four inches deep that reaches half down the hall.» Nobody measured those tears in litres. The clues are the pool and the hall, so gallons means a very large amount.
fact: A gallon is a unit for measuring liquids.
fact: In the UK (imperial system), 1 gallon = 4 quarts = 8 pints, and it is about 4.55 litres.
fact: A US gallon is about 3.79 litres, so it is a bit smaller than a UK gallon.
fact: «Gallons of tears» means a very large amount of tears, not an exact measurement.
fact: Words like this are an exaggeration: they make something sound much bigger than it really is.
exercise: In the UK, how many pints make one gallon? | 4 | 12 | *8 | 6
exercise: «She sheds gallons of tears.» What does gallons mean here? | Exactly 4.55 litres of tears | *A very large amount | A few drops | A small bottle
exercise: Which holds more liquid: a UK gallon or a US gallon? | They hold exactly the same amount | A US gallon, about 3.79 litres | A pint | *A UK gallon, about 4.55 litres
test: A gallon is a unit for measuring what? | *Liquids, such as milk or petrol | The length of a road | Solid rocks | Time
test: Mum says, «I've told you gallons of times!» What does she mean? | *She has said it a very large number of times | She measured the times in litres | She has never said it at all | She has told you exactly four times
exam: Jayden says a gallon is always the same size everywhere. Is he right? | Yes, a gallon is 4 litres everywhere | *No, a US gallon is smaller, about 3.79 litres | No, a gallon is a measure of time | Yes, a gallon is always 8 litres
